UPDATE companies SET description='The company describes itself as "car guys through and through," focused on building custom vehicles and composite parts that benefit the client or market.

The company designs and manufactures a line of composite automotive components, including hand-laid FRP and infused carbon-fiber parts such as dash panels, wide-body kits, grilles, and diffusers for platforms like the Nissan S14, Chevrolet Corvette C6, and Nissan R35. Through its Big Builds program, Mop Top Pros completes full custom vehicle projects—examples include a Mitsubishi EVO-X, a Chevrolet Corvette C6, and a Chevrolet C-10—handling 3D modeling, virtual rendering, fabrication, and in-house finishing such as powder coating, paint, and upholstery.

Its Big Builds program targets owners of platforms such as the Mitsubishi EVO, Chevrolet Corvette, and Chevrolet C-10 who want a turnkey custom build with selectable options.

The founder emphasizes an imaginative design approach and fabrication precision to create vehicles that stand out while maintaining performance. The Big Builds program is positioned as offering faster turnaround and lower cost than traditional custom builds while still allowing customer-selected options.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["3D modeling", "Virtual rendering", "Fabrication", "Composite manufacturing (hand-laid FRP)", "Composite manufacturing (infused carbon fiber)", "Powder coating", "Painting", "Upholstery", "Custom vehicle builds", "Composite part design", "Automotive styling"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Custom car building", "Performance automotive", "Show car building"], "materials": ["FRP (fiberglass reinforced plastic)", "Carbon fiber"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house finish work: powder coating, paint, upholstery", "3D modeling and virtual rendering before fabrication", "Big Builds program with faster turnaround and lower cost", "Hand-laid FRP and infused carbon-fiber composite parts", "Proprietary composite product line designed and manufactured in-house"], "facts_used": ["Location: Mandan, ND -> /", "Composite parts: hand-laid FRP, infused carbon fiber -> /", "Specific parts: s14 dash, c6 wide, a35 grill, r35 diff -> /", "Big Builds program: Mitsubishi EVO-X, Chevrolet Corvette C6, Chevrolet C-10 -> /", "Services: 3D modeling, virtual rendering, fabrication, powder coating, paint, upholstery -> /", "Founder quote: ''Building cars has always intrigued me...'' -> /", "Differentiators: faster turnaround, lower cost, customer options -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From our Product Line to our Big Build Program we utilize our creative eye for Automotive Design to dial in 3d-models. Virtual rendering gives you a first hand look at the concept before we began fabrication... Even the finish work we take care of in house, Powdercoating, Paint, Upholstery etc..", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mop-top-pros' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Samvardhana Motherson Reflectec (SMR) operates its North American hub in Warren, Michigan, as part of the Motherson Group founded in 1975. The group grew into one of the 22 largest automotive suppliers worldwide, though the INPUT does not specify the ownership structure or individual founders.

SMR develops and manufactures rear-view mirror systems and intelligent camera technologies for automakers. Its manufacturing portfolio spans design, simulation, prototyping, tooling, moulding, painting and final assembly of integrated modules, from simple plastic components to complex assemblies with surfaces and embedded electrical functions. The company employs more than 10,400 people globally and holds a 24 percent share of the worldwide exterior-mirror market.

The division supplies nearly every major automotive manufacturer across North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, providing interior and exterior mirrors as well as camera-based environment sensors.

