echnologies for the automotive industry", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "10,400+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='motherson-warren' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Motherson Yachiyo Automotive Tech Products of America, Inc. operates from Columbus, Ohio. The business became part of the Motherson group in 2024, extending a track record as a Tier 1 automotive supplier that dates back to 1997.

The company designs and manufactures plastic fuel tanks and sunroofs, with sunroof production described as its flagship operation. An Ecoat (electrodeposition) coating line handles steel (galvannealed or zinc-plated) and aluminum parts, with a tunnel opening of 3 by 4 by 3 feet. The firm also offers sub-assembly services to simplify customers’ workflows.

Its customer base is the automotive industry, where it serves as a Tier 1 supplier.

