UPDATE companies SET description='Mountain High Woodworks was founded in 1980 in the Bridger Mountains near Bozeman, Montana. The company remains based in Bozeman, where it operates a full-service woodworking shop.

The shop produces custom cabinetry, furniture, millwork, and doors, blending state-of-the-art CNC machining with traditional hand carving. In-house capabilities extend to custom metal blacksmithing, leaded hand-blown glass, ironwork, and leather detailing. Design engineers create CAD shop drawings for client approval, and the finish department develops custom finishes on sample pieces before full production. All manufacturing occurs at the Bozeman facility.

The firm serves architects, builders, and interior designers across the Mountain West and beyond, with projects completed in Montana, Wyoming, Idaho, Utah, Colorado, Arizona, Ohio, Nevada, California, Alaska, Canada, Mexico, South Korea, and Quebec. Clients range from owners of small custom cabins to large luxury residences, and the portfolio includes specialty spaces such as gun rooms, fly-fishing rooms, trophy rooms, saloon bars, wine cellars, smoking rooms, and home theaters.

Mountain High Woodworks emphasizes a complete custom-shop experience, from concept through installation. The company highlights its combination of advanced CNC technology and hand craftsmanship, the ability to integrate diverse materials, and a team of seasoned installers who ensure the final fit matches the design intent.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry", "Custom furniture", "Custom millwork", "Custom doors", "Custom woodworking", "Custom cabinetry design and engineering", "CNC machining", "Hand carving", "Custom finishing", "Custom metal blacksmithing", "Leaded hand-blown glass fabrication", "Ironwork (Old Iron)", "Leather working", "CAD shop drawings", "Sample building", "Installation services"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Architecture", "Interior design", "Specialty room construction"], "materials": ["Wood", "Metal", "Glass", "Iron", "Leather"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complete custom-shop experience from design through installation", "State-of-the-art CNC machining combined with hand carving", "In-house custom metalwork, glass, and leather integration", "CAD shop drawings for client review and approval", "Seasoned installers ensuring design intent and fit"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1980 -> db", "Headquarters Bozeman, Montana -> db", "Custom cabinetry, furniture, millwork, doors -> /", "CNC machining and hand carving capabilities -> /", "Custom metal blacksmithing, leaded glass, iron, leather -> /", "Design engineering with CAD shop drawings -> /", "Sample building and custom finish approvals -> /", "Installation by seasoned installers -> /", "Serves architects, builders, interior designers -> /", "Projects across Western US, Canada, Mexico, South Korea, Quebec -> /", "Specialty spaces: gun rooms, fly fishing rooms, trophy rooms, saloon rooms, wine rooms, smoking rooms, theater rooms -> /", "Complete custom shop experience -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The manufacturing process happens at our shop here in Bozeman, Montana.", "founded_year": "1980", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mountain-high-woodworks-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mr. Plastic operates from Jonesboro, Arkansas, with additional locations in Little Rock and Fort Smith. The company is family-owned, though its founding year and founders are not publicly disclosed. The business began as a local plastics store serving central Arkansas.

The company distributes a wide range of plastic rod, sheet, and tube stock, covering engineering plastics to sign plastics, and provides custom fabrication services. It emphasizes no minimum order requirements, no cutting fees, and weekly free delivery to customers in the region. The staff collectively brings over 50 years of combined experience in customized and engineered plastics.

Mr. Plastic serves industrial, engineering, and signage sectors, supplying materials for applications ranging from industrial components to sign fabrication.

