UPDATE companies SET description='Mrs. Clark''s Foods operates from Ankeny, Iowa, where it was founded in 1926 by Mary Clark as a small mayonnaise supplier to local grocery chains. Over nearly a century, the company has expanded its portfolio to include juices, salad dressings, and a full range of condiments while remaining rooted in its original Midwestern location.

The company runs dedicated manufacturing facilities focused on hot-fill juice, cold-fill BBQ sauce, and emulsified products such as mayonnaise and dressings. Its 200,000-square-foot warehouse supports dry, refrigerated, and frozen storage, and the operation produced 4.5 million cases in the most recent year with a reported 97 percent yield and 99.7 percent forecasted fulfillment.

Mrs. Clark''s serves global and regional brands across consumer retail, private label, co-manufacturing, and food-service channels. Customers engage the company for turnkey co-packing, white-label production, formulation development, and national-brand-equivalent matching, with packaging options ranging from single-serve cups and sachets to bulk pails, drums, and totes.

The business emphasizes a quality heritage and operational consistency, citing pillars such as ''A Higher Bar'' and ''Consistency to Grow'' alongside a delivery radius of one day within 600 miles and two days within 1,200 miles. Its stated mission is to partner with brands on innovative food and beverage solutions that meet current needs and anticipate future demand.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF','GFSi']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Co-packing (turnkey and tolling)", "Food service manufacturing", "Private brand development", "White label manufacturing", "Hot-fill juice production (concentrate, not-from-concentrate, nectars, coffee syrups)", "Cold-fill BBQ sauce production", "High-shear mixing", "Blending & homogenization", "Emulsification", "Product development", "Ingredient sourcing", "Label support", "Production & logistics", "QA testing", "Production reporting", "Export facilitation", "Warehousing (dry, refrigerated, frozen)", "Order fulfillment", "Bulk packaging (pails, drums, totes)", "Single-serve packaging (cups, pouches, sachets)", "Formulation review", "Branding & packaging design", "Go-to-market strategy", "National brand equivalent matching"], "industries": ["Food and beverage", "Consumer packaged goods", "Private label", "Co-manufacturing", "Food service"], "materials": ["Fruit concentrates", "Not-from-concentrate juices", "Nectars", "Coffee syrups", "Mayonnaise ingredients", "Salad dressing ingredients", "BBQ sauce ingredients"], "equipment": ["Mixing stations & kettles", "Liquefier", "Hot fill juice line", "Cold fill BBQ sauce line", "Emulsification equipment", "High-shear mixing equipment"], "volume": "4.5 million cases annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["99.7% forecasted fulfillment rate", "4.5 million cases produced annually", "97% production yield", "200,000 sq ft multi-temperature warehouse", "SQF and GFSi certified facilities"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1926 by Mary Clark in Iowa -> /about", "Headquarters Ankeny, Iow