UPDATE companies SET description='NZK Plastics LLC was founded in 1996 by Nick Karnavas, a Penn State University graduate with a B.S. in Chemical Engineering, in North Versailles Township, Pennsylvania, just outside Pittsburgh. The company began with a single injection molding machine and has since expanded to operate seven machines with clamp tonnages ranging from 50 to 400 tons.

The shop provides custom injection molding services supported by in-house tool development, part design using CAD, rapid prototyping via 3D printing, and secondary operations such as sonic and solvent welding. Its seven molding machines handle single- and multi-cavity molds, and the company reports more than 600 completed projects over 25-plus years.

Customers span automotive, medical device, consumer electronics, and renewable energy sectors. Testimonials cite work for automotive and medical device manufacturers, as well as a consumer electronics client who credited the team with material selection and design modifications that reduced cost.

The company states its mission is to deliver top-quality custom injection molding solutions with a customer-first approach, aiming to be the Pittsburgh region''s provider of innovative, high-quality injection molding services. It emphasizes a state-of-the-art quality control department and the integration of 3D printing with injection molding for rapid prototyping.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (50-400 ton clamp force)", "Rapid prototyping (3D printing)", "Part design with CAD", "Custom tool development (single and multi-cavity molds)", "Sonic welding", "Solvent welding", "Quality assurance/inspection"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical Devices", "Renewable Energy", "Consumer Electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (50-400 ton clamp force)", "3D printing equipment for rapid prototyping"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customer-first approach to custom injection molding", "In-house tool development for single and multi-cavity molds", "Integration of 3D printing with injection molding for rapid prototyping", "Secondary operations including sonic and solvent welding", "Seven injection molding machines ranging from 50 to 400 tons clamp force"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 by Nick Karnavas (Penn State B.S. Chemical Engineering) -> /", "Started with one injection molding machine, now operates 7 machines 50-400 tons -> /", "Headquartered in North Versailles Township, Pennsylvania -> /", "Services: injection molding, rapid prototyping, part design with CAD, tooling capabilities, secondary operations (sonic welding, solvent welding) -> /", "600+ projects completed, 25+ years experience -> /", "Industries served: automotive, medical devices, renewable energy, consumer electronics -> /", "Mission: deliver top-quality custom injection molding solutions with customer-first approach -> /", "Vision: be Pittsburgh''s leading provider of innovative, high-quality injection molding services -> /", "State-of-the-art QC department mentioned -> /", "Partnered with Smithers for environmental management systems certification -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "NZK Plastics, LLC specializes in custom injection molding solutions.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nzk-plastics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Nagakura Engineering Works operates from Columbus, Indiana, as the U.S. base of a company founded in 1950 in Shizuoka, Japan. The business began with research into cold forging technology and has since expanded to production sites in the United States, Vietnam, and Mexico.

The company specializes in cold forging, producing more than 30 million parts annually for automotive applications. Its portfolio includes transmission components, motor and hybrid-vehicle parts, and what it describes as the world''s longest cold forged shafts at 700 millimeters. Nagakura develops its own machine specifications and applies continuous improvement (Kaizen) to its equipment.

Customers are primarily in the automotive sector, including transmission manufacturers such as ZF, for which Nagakura has supported development of new generation transmissions. Parts ship globally to automakers and tier-one suppliers.

