UPDATE companies SET description='Nashville Sheet Metal was founded in 2003 in Nashville, Tennessee. The company is now owned by Dexter Cross, who joined as an estimator and project manager in 2014 after graduating from Tennessee Technological University with a degree in manufacturing engineering technology. Cross assumed ownership after progressing through the organization.

The firm operates a full-service production shop providing HVAC ductwork fabrication, specialty fabrication and installation, custom design, industrial sheet metal services, and pre-construction services. Its capabilities extend to building information modeling (BIM) and coordination using Revit and Trimble technologies, field measuring, welding, and stainless steel fabrication for food manufacturing equipment. A shop manager oversees a crew of welders and fabricators.

The company serves commercial, industrial, and specialty food manufacturing clients across the Middle Tennessee region. Projects include architectural and roofing sheet metal, HVAC systems, and custom stainless steel installations for food processing facilities.

