UPDATE companies SET description='Neocera LLC is headquartered in Beltsville, Maryland. The company was founded in 1989 by Dr. Venkatesan as a commercial vehicle for pulsed laser deposition (PLD) technology, focusing on complex multi-component metal-oxide thin film materials.

Neocera designs and manufactures pulsed laser deposition (PLD) systems, pulsed electron deposition (PED) systems, related components, and in-situ real-time diagnostic tools for thin-film development. The company describes itself as the largest supplier of PLD and PED tools for research and development, with experience integrating its systems with other deposition technologies and analytical equipment to create custom solutions.

The company serves academia (universities), government (national research laboratories), and multinational corporations (corporate R&D centers). Its systems are installed in over 30 countries worldwide, supporting research and industrial applications in advanced materials.

Neocera states its mission is to become researchers'' and manufacturers'' first choice for PLD and PED equipment. The firm remains active in materials research, the application of PLD into new material systems and managing the transition of PLD processes from the laboratory to the industrial marketplace. Pulsed Electron Deposition was added as a complementary technique in 2001.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pulsed Laser Deposition (PLD)", "Pulsed Electron Deposition (PED)", "In-situ real-time diagnostics", "Thin-film process development", "Custom system integration", "Component manufacturing for PLD/PED systems"], "industries": ["Academia", "Government research", "Multinational corporations", "Universities", "National laboratories", "Corporate R&D"], "materials": ["Complex multi-component metal-oxide thin film materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest supplier of PLD and PED tools for R&D", "Pioneer in PLD technology since 1989", "In-situ real-time diagnostic capabilities", "Custom integration with other deposition and analytical systems", "Installed base in over 30 countries"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1989 by Dr. Venkatesan -> /about", "Headquarters in Beltsville, Maryland -> /", "Manufactures PLD and PED systems, components, and in-situ diagnostic tools -> /", "Largest supplier of PLD/PED tools for R&D -> /", "Systems installed in over 30 countries -> /about", "Added Pulsed Electron Deposition (PED) in 2001 -> /about", "Serves academia, government, multinational companies -> /", "Mission to become researchers'' and manufacturers'' first choice for PLD/PED equipment -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Neocera offers a full range of solutions for thin films including pulsed laser deposition (PLD) systems, pulsed electron deposition (PED) systems, components and in situ diagnostic tools.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='neocera-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Neodesha Plastics Inc. was founded in 1969 by Kenneth W. Peitz in Neodesha, Kansas. The family-owned company began in a 10,000-square-foot facility and has since expanded to over 165,000 square feet of production space in Southeast Kansas. It remains under Peitz family ownership with a long-tenured workforce.

The company provides full-service custom plastic manufacturing, including thermoforming (vacuum and pressure forming, deep-draw, twin-spindle rotary), CNC plastic machining (3-axis and 5-axis), rotational molding, plastic prototyping, and turnkey assembly and kitting. Its vertically integrated operation handles projects from one-off prototypes to runs of 10,000 finished goods, offering design-for-manufacturability feedback, tooling guidance, and material selection support.

Neodesha Plastics serves OEMs across automotive and transportation (instrument panels, chrome-laminated trims, modular kits), medical and life sciences (sterilizable housings, portable enclosures), marine and outdoor (UV-stable enclosures, fluid tanks, cup holders), and industrial and consumer markets (machine guards, trays, displays, ruggedized enclosures). Its central location enables shorter shipping timelines to the Midwest and beyond.

