UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Dalton Gardens, Idaho, with a showroom in nearby Coeur d''Alene, North Idaho Log Furniture Company was founded in 1996 by Dan and Kelli Booterbaugh. The couple started the business as a small mountain workshop driven by a shared passion for woodworking and the outdoors.

The company handcrafts solid-wood log furniture for every room: beds, bunk beds, tables, chairs, dressers, cabinets, desks, nightstands, couches, mantels, and lamps. Using Lodgepole Pine, Ponderosa Pine, and Hickory harvested from North Idaho forests, each log is hand-selected, hand-peeled, sanded, and joined with traditional mortise-and-tenon construction. Finishes are eco-conscious stains and protective oils. The shop builds custom pieces to order and constructs custom pallets for each shipment, calculating freight individually rather than using a cart-based checkout.

The company serves homeowners, cabin builders, and interior designers across the United States. Customers range from individuals furnishing mountain cabins and lakeside retreats to design professionals specifying rustic pieces for residential projects.

The founders emphasize three principles: quality, integrity, and authenticity. They position their work as a continuation of Idaho craftsmanship, highlighting hand-built joinery, responsible sourcing, and a made-to-order model that avoids mass production. The goal is furniture that "lives with you" for generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted log furniture manufacturing", "Custom furniture design and build", "Mortise-and-tenon joinery", "Hand-peeling and sanding of logs", "Premium oil finishing", "Custom pallet construction for shipping", "Personal freight calculation"], "industries": ["Homeowners", "Cabin builders", "Interior designers"], "materials": ["Lodgepole Pine", "Ponderosa Pine", "Hickory", "Eco-conscious stains", "Protective coatings"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted using mortise-and-tenon joinery rather than mass-production shortcuts", "Timber responsibly sourced from North Idaho forests (Lodgepole Pine, Ponderosa Pine, Hickory)", "Every piece built to custom dimensions and specifications", "Shipping calculated per order with custom-built pallets for heavy items"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 by Dan and Kelli Booterbaugh -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Dalton Gardens, Idaho (db); showroom in Coeur d''Alene -> /about-us", "Handcrafted log furniture using Lodgepole Pine, Ponderosa Pine, Hickory -> /about-us", "Mortise-and-tenon joinery, hand-peeling, sanding, oil finishing -> /about-us", "Custom pieces, custom pallets, personal shipping calculation -> /", "Serves homeowners, cabin builders, designers -> /about-us", "Principles: quality, integrity, authenticity -> /about-us", "No mass production, responsible sourcing, eco-conscious finishes -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Each table, bed, and chair we build carries the rugged soul of Idaho''s forests and the precision of true American craftsmanship.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='north-idaho-log-furniture-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='NorthWoods Manufacturing was founded in 2005 in Lancaster, New Hampshire. The company operates as a custom cabinet shop serving residential and commercial clients across northern New Hampshire, northern Vermont, and western Massachusetts.

The shop produces custom kitchens, bathroom vanities, countertops, and closet systems, and also offers CNC machining services for cabinet components. With a team of eleven skilled craftsmen, NorthWoods uses computer-controlled equipment to cut and fabricate parts, supplying both finished cabinets shipped throughout the United States and Canada and raw components to other cabinet shops that outsource cutting to control costs and quality.

Customers range from local homeowners and custom builders to commercial contractors; notable projects include a kitchenette for North Country Ford in Lancaster, cabinetry for Weeks Medical Center, and CNC-machined parts for B.O.H. Interiors. The company also partners with cabinet shops nationwide that rely on NorthWoods for precision-cut components.

NorthWoods emphasizes that all products are manufactured in its Lancaster facility, positioning itself as a one-stop source for design, fabrication, and delivery. The business grew from a focus on thoughtful, affordable design and aims to give clients a kitchen they “love,” not just one they are happy with.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinet manufacturing", "CNC machining", "Cabinet component cutting", "Kitchen and bath design", "Commercial cabinetry", "Countertop fabrication", "Closet systems"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Healthcare", "Automotive", "Interior design", "Cabinet manufacturing (supply chain)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All products manufactured in Lancaster, NH", "Computer-controlled equipment for precision cabinet component cutting", "Finished cabinets shipped throughout the US and Canada", "Supplies cabinet components to other custom shops nationwide", "Free in-home design consultation for residential projects"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 -> db", "Headquarters Lancaster, NH -> db", "Custom cabinet shop specializing in residential kitchens and baths as well as commercial cabinetry -> /about-us", "Employs eleven local residents -> /about-us", "All products made in Lancaster, NH -> /about-us", "Ships finished cabinets throughout US and Canada -> /about-us", "Supplies cabinet components to other custom shops -> /about-us", "CNC machining services for kitchen parts -> / (testimonial from Jorge Oliveira)", "Serves residential homeowners, contractors, custom builders in Northern VT and NH -> /about-us", "Commercial projects in NH, VT, MA -> /about-us", "Customer examples: Barbara Rossell (residential), Keith Kopp of North Country Ford (commercial), Jorge Oliveira of B.O.H. Interiors (CNC machining) -> /", "Weeks Medical Center listed as industry served -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "NorthWoods Manufacturing is a custom cabinet shop specializing in residential kitchens and baths as well as commercial cabinetry.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "11", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='northwoods-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Northeast Fabricators & Mechanical Services operates from a 32,000-square-foot facility in Dalton, Massachusetts, at Ashuelot Park. The company was formed in February 2001 and has grown from a two-person operation to a team of 19 skilled craftsmen, including welders, pipers, millwrights, and mechanics.

The shop provides full-service welding and metal fabrication, offering in-house production and on-site field support. Capabilities span high-definition CNC plasma cutting, structural welding (MIG, TIG, stick, soldering, brazing), metal forming, piping, shearing, sawing, drilling, tapping, pipe bending, and heavy equipment rebuilds. The team works with steel, stainless steel, mild steel, aluminum, and various tubing profiles, using CAD/CAM design support to turn prints into finished parts such as custom tanks, armor plates, water filtration equipment, pump skids, and chemical dosing systems.

Customers include paper mills, construction firms, industrial and commercial clients across Western Massachusetts, and defense-sector buyers requiring armor plates, gas tanks, and other specialty fabrications. The company also builds commercial snow plow frames, trailer rebuilds, retail display racks, and custom signage.

Leadership emphasizes craftsmanship, innovative solutions, reliability, and responsiveness as the foundation of its reputation. The mission centers on maintaining state-of-the-art equipment, fostering teamwork, and investing in tools that enable the highest quality work, with a stated goal of 100 percent customer satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High Definition CNC Plasma Cutting", "Welding (MIG, TIG, Stick, Soldering, Brazing)", "Structural Welding by Certified Welders", "Metal Forming", "Piping", "Shearing and Sawing", "Drilling and Tapping", "Pipe Bending", "Heavy Equipment Structural Rebuilds and Modifications", "Commercial Snow Plow and Frame Repair", "Trailer Rebuilds", "Bracket Fabrication", "Custom Commercial and Retail Display Racks and Dollies", "Custom Sign Fabrication", "Defense Specialties (Armor Plates, Gas Tanks)", "Stainless Steel Water Filtration Equipment Fabrication", "Mechanical Installation / Equipment Mounting / Piping", "Containerized System Production / Custom Tanks", "Waste Water Components", "Chemical Dosing Systems", "Pump Skids", "CAD/CAM Design Services"], "industries": ["Defense", "Paper Manufacturing", "Construction", "Industrial", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Mild Steel", "Aluminum", "Angle Iron", "Round Tubing", "Square Tubing"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["32,000 sq ft shop with state-of-the-art equipment", "In-house production and complete on-site field support", "Multi-disciplined crew of certified welders, pipers, millwrights, and mechanics", "CAD/CAM design support for custom fabrication", "Defense specialties including armor plates and gas tanks"], "facts_used": ["Company formed February 2001 -> /about", "Grown from two to nineteen employees -> /about", "Located at Ashuelot Park in Dalton, MA -> /about", "32,000 square foot shop -> /", "Full service welding and metal fabrication -> /", "In-house production and complete on-site support -> /", "High Definition CNC Plasma Cutting -> /", "Welding (MIG, TIG, Stick, Soldering, Brazing) -> /", "Metal Forming, Piping, Shearing, Sawing, Drilling, Tapping, Pipe Bending -> /", "Heavy Equipment Structural Rebuilds and Modifications -> /", "Commercial Snow Plow and Frame Repair -> /", "Trailer Rebuilds -> /", "Custom Display Racks and Dollies -> /", "Custom Signs -> /", "Defense Specialties (Armor Plates/Gas Tanks) -> /", "Stainless Steel Water Filtration Equipment -> /", "Mechanical Installation/Equipment Mounting/Piping -> /", "Containerized System Production/Custom Tanks -> /", "Waste Water Components -> /", "Chemical Dosing Systems -> /", "Pump Skids -> /", "Materials: steel, stainless steel, mild steel, aluminum, angle iron, round tubing, square tubing -> /", "CAD/CAM design support -> /", "Serves paper mills, construction sites, industrial and commercial clients -> /", "Goal of 100% customer satisfaction, craftsmanship, innovative solutions, reliability, responsiveness -> /about", "State-of-the-art equipment, teamwork, purchasing tools for best job -> /about", "Member of Berkshire Chambers of Commerce and Associated Industries of Massachusetts -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a full service welding and metal fabrication company with over 40 years of experience.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "19", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='northeast-fabricators-mechanical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Northeast Foreign Cars operates in White River Junction, Vermont, and has served the Upper Valley region of Vermont and New Hampshire since 1981.

The company provides auto repair, general maintenance, and auto parts sales, along with a selection of used foreign and domestic cars. Services include check-engine diagnostics, oil changes, tire rotations and balancing, tune-ups, and emissions maintenance. The parts inventory covers brakes, suspensions, gaskets, filters, and other maintenance and wear items, with common items kept in stock and dealer parts ordered as needed. Facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

Customers are primarily passenger-vehicle owners in the Upper Valley area of Vermont and New Hampshire.

